>>>>> On 19 May 93 18:02:32 GMT, mke@qiclab.scn.rain.com (Mike Miller) said:

Mike> BTW, I wonder how many of the people who are really succesfull
Mike> are playing on UNIX were cheating is a bit more of a challenge.
Mike> (If it can be done at all, I haven't tried.)

It's almost as hard to figure out how to cheat on a properly
configured Unix system, as it is to win the game honestly.  NetHack
3.1.1 is very popular with old timers, as well as new players.  It is
one of the new players who top the highscore list, and noone has won
yet.  This is how it should be.

I have played Hack since version 1.0.2, and 3.1.1 is easely the best
version ever.  The new challanges (like monsters using wands) can be
overcome with appropriate strategies, and finding those strategies is
what the game is all about (and has always been, since the first
version of rogue).

Since the game now implements checkpoints, maybe it should offer you
to continue from the last checkpoint after you get killed, in a
non-scoring mode?  This would allow people who hate the game and want
to finish it fast to do so, even on UNIX.  And it would be more
convenient for PC users than copying save files.

What do people think about this idea?


